@startuml
title The R2 bounded-read path - four read opcodes, the 11-word core header, the read-count ceiling
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f8f8f8
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666
hide stereotype

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<ops>> #dbe5f1
  BorderColor<<ops>> #6c8ebf
  FontColor<<ops>> #1f3864
  BackgroundColor<<hdr>> #e5d8f7
  BorderColor<<hdr>> #9673a6
  FontColor<<hdr>> #4a235a
  BackgroundColor<<live>> #d5e8d4
  BorderColor<<live>> #82b366
  FontColor<<live>> #1d4620
  BackgroundColor<<ceil>> #ffe6cc
  BorderColor<<ceil>> #d79b00
  FontColor<<ceil>> #7f4b00
  BackgroundColor<<refuse>> #f8cecc
  BorderColor<<refuse>> #b85450
  FontColor<<refuse>> #7b1c18
}

package "R2 closed the 'observe' half - four opcodes, and only ONE of them may be asked live" {
  component "0x12 READ_CPU\n  request  len 0\n  response 7 words\n\nTHE ONLY NON-HALTING READ\nanswers while run = 1, which is\nthe entire point of the opcode:\na debugger must see a running\nprogram. Answers from registers\nin the request's own CRC cycle,\nso it emits ZERO wait words." as rdcpu <<live>>

  component "0x13 READ_IMEM\n  request  (address, count)\n  address = WORD index\n  count   = WORDS, ascending\n\nNOT_READY while run = 1, no fault." as rdimem <<ops>>

  component "0x14 READ_DMEM\n  request  (address, count)\n  address = BYTE index\n  count   = BYTES, ascending\n  TWO BYTES PER RESPONSE WORD,\n  HIGH BYTE FIRST (big-endian\n  within the word)\n\nNOT_READY while run = 1, no fault." as rdmem <<ops>>

  component "0x15 DUMP_CORE\n  request  len 0\n  response THE 11-WORD HEADER,\n  word for word, while STOPPED\n\nNOT_READY while run = 1, no fault." as dumpecor <<ops>>

  rdcpu --> rdimem : the read port arbitrates\nthe CPU address buses
  rdimem --> rdmem
  rdmem --> dumpecor
}

package "THE 11-WORD CORE HEADER - STATUS 0x11 and DUMP_CORE 0x15 return it identically" {
  component "w0   STATUS CODE\nOK / BUSY / BAD_FRAME / RANGE /\nFAULT / UNSUPPORTED / NOT_READY" as h0 <<hdr>>
  component "w1   STATE\n2 bits in the LOW half, upper 14 ZERO\n0 STOPPED   1 RUNNING\n2 DEBUG_HOLD   3 BP_HIT\nR2's old 0/1 keep their meaning;\n2/3 are new and only debug control\ncan enter them" as h1 <<hdr>>
  component "w2   RUN\n1 bit, the STRAP level, not a\nhost-bus register" as h2 <<hdr>>
  component "w3   TARGET\nthe selected target, echoed" as h3 <<hdr>>
  component "w4   PC  -  FULL WIDTH\n10 bits (PCW in a 1,024-word\nmachine), upper 6 ZERO.\nThe old 8-bit dbg_pc truncation\nHAD TO GO" as h4 <<hdr>>
  component "w5   A   -  8 bits\nThe ISA is the source of truth and\nno field is invented, so A STAYS\n8 bits even though the host's\nFakePE modelled 13" as h5 <<hdr>>
  component "w6   X   -  8 bits" as h6 <<hdr>>
  component "w7   Y   -  8 bits" as h7 <<hdr>>
  component "w8   TIMER  -  8 bits" as h8 <<hdr>>
  component "w9   FAULTS  -  sticky bits\n0x0001 FAULT_LOAD    run abort\n0x0002 FAULT_CRC     bad frame CRC\n0x0004 FAULT_RANGE   an out-of-range read\n0x0008 FAULT_PROTOCOL bad length/header,\nor a word truncated by CS_N rising\nCLEARED BY 0x16 CLEAR_FAULT" as h9 <<refuse>>
  component "w10  WORDS_WRITTEN\nthe LOAD commit counter - the\nvectors assume 3 because a real\n3-word LOAD established it, so the\nnumber is never poked in" as h10 <<hdr>>

  h0 --> h1
  h1 --> h2
  h2 --> h3
  h3 --> h4
  h4 --> h5
  h5 --> h6
  h6 --> h7
  h7 --> h8
  h8 --> h9
  h9 --> h10
}

package "READ_CPU is a DIFFERENT SHAPE - 7 words, and it is the only place 'insn' appears" {
  component "w0  STATUS CODE  OK\nw1  PC   10 bits, full width\nw2  A    8 bits\nw3  X    8 bits\nw4  Y    8 bits\nw5  INSN  16 bits, the LATCHED word\nw6  RUN  the strap level" as r7 <<live>>
}

package "THE READ-COUNT CEILING CONTRACT - one frame carries 15, and that is a contract, not a limit to discover" {
  component "WHERE 15 COMES FROM\nresp_buf is 16 slots.\nSlot 0 is the status word,\nso 15 slots carry DATA.\nMAX_READ_WORDS = 15." as c1 <<ceil>>

  component "READ_IMEM  count in WORDS\ncount  1 .. 15   accepted\ncount  16+       RANGE" as c2 <<ceil>>

  component "READ_DMEM  count in BYTES\ncount  1 .. 30   accepted\n(two bytes per word,\n so ceil(count/2) data words)\ncount  31+       RANGE" as c3 <<ceil>>

  component "count == 0 IS RANGE, DELIBERATELY\nnot a zero-length OK frame. An empty\nread is a host bug, and answering OK\nwith no words would leave the host\nunable to tell 'nothing requested' from\n'read refused'. Pinned by the\nread_ceiling_and_zero_count vector." as c4 <<ceil>>

  component "OVERSIZE IS RANGE SO THE HOST SPLITS\nthe transfer - it is never silently\ntruncated, and never wrapped." as c5 <<ceil>>

  component "OUT OF RANGE IS RANGE + STICKY\naddress+count past the end is RANGE,\nNEVER A WRAPPED READ, and latches\nFAULT_RANGE 0x0004 exactly like a\nwrite does. CLEAR_FAULT clears it." as c6 <<refuse>>

  component "THE BOUNDS ARE CHECKED BEFORE ANY\nREAD IS ISSUED, so a rejected read\nnever touches memory at all." as c7 <<ceil>>
}

package "THE ASYMMETRY A DEBUGGER MUST NOT GET WRONG" {
  component "A REFUSAL IS NOT A HOLD\nDUMP_CORE is gated on IF (run), not on\nIF (dbg_hold_r). With the strap HIGH the\ncore is stopped in the debug sense and\nDUMP_CORE must STILL refuse.\n\nProved by mutation: re-gating DUMP_CORE on\nthe hold instead of the strap drops the\nconformance to 6/22 - it is the step that\ncatches it, not an assertion." as asym <<refuse>>

  component "AND THE OPPOSITE ASYMMETRY\nbounded reads are NOT_READY while run=1\nwith NO FAULT - a sequencing rejection,\nexactly like LOAD while running. So a\nrefusal latches nothing, and a host that\ntries again after stopping the core gets\na clean answer with no cleanup needed." as asym2 <<refuse>>
}

' LAYOUT ONLY, no architecture. The five sections read in order - the opcodes,
' then the header they return, then READ_CPU's different shape, then the
' ceiling, then the asymmetry - but as siblings they lay out as columns and the
' diagram goes wide. This hidden chain stacks them so each section adds height
' rather than width, which is the squarer-aspect invariant in
' diagrams/README.md. Safe to delete.
dumpecor -[hidden]down-> h0
h10 -[hidden]down-> r7

note bottom of rdcpu
  READ_CPU IS THE ONE OP A DEBUGGER CAN
  POLL ON A RUNNING CORE, and it is also the
  one that reports insn. The subtlety, and
  the reason this is drawn separately from
  the 11-word header: insn is NOT
  unconditionally imem[pc]. pe_cpu fetches
  at next_pc while EXECUTING, at pc while
  HELD, and at 0 at the boot stop. A
  free-running readback therefore reports the
  LANDING word, and at a freeze it reports
  the LATCHED pipeline word. A harness that
  synthesises a mid-execution snapshot
  collapses that fetch pipeline, so its insn
  is the collapsed one - a TESTBENCH
  artefact, not an RTL disagreement.
  Evidence: R3-DEBUG-CONTROL-CONTRACT.md
  section 3, notes for the vector author.
end note

note bottom of h4
  THE WIDTH CHANGE IS THE POINT OF R2, NOT A
  DETAIL. STATUS now carries pc/a/x/y/timer
  at NATIVE widths and READ_CPU answers
  while run=1, so the P3 liveness gap is
  closed on the chip side: a host can
  actually see a running program. The
  manager ruled the ISA is the source of
  truth, which is why A stayed 8 bits and
  the host model's 13-bit A was a MODEL BUG.
end note

note bottom of h9
  FAULTS IS STICKY AND READ-BACK, so a host
  sees a latched fault in the SAME header it
  uses for registers. A sticky bit is not
  cleared by a good read, and an
  out-of-range READ latches exactly like a
  write - so a host that probes past the end
  once must call CLEAR_FAULT before its next
  STATUS looks clean.
end note

note bottom of c4
  TWO OF THE THREE REAL DEFECTS R2 FOUND WERE
  IN EXACTLY THIS AREA, which is why the
  ceiling is drawn as a contract: an ODD DMEM
  BYTE COUNT DROPPED ITS TRAILING BYTE (held
  in a half-word register and never emitted,
  leaving the response a word short of its
  declared length), and the RESPONSE LAUNCH
  NEVER FIRED because it sat inside an arm
  that the launch itself cleared. A third
  left an X on the MISO pad before the first
  frame, which the pad-level TB caught. None
  of the three was visible from a spec.
end note

note bottom of asym
  THIS IS THE SAME ASYMMETRY THE HOST-SIDE
  MODEL CANNOT SHOW. A host model reaches a
  held state by declaring debug_hold: true;
  the CHIP reaches it by traffic, and the
  traffic has to be legal. That is why the
  held-core vectors had to DRIVE the debug
  opcodes on the real pe_ctrl to build their
  pre-state rather than forcing the
  registers - the states 2 and 3 exist only
  if the opcodes can produce them.
end note

legend left
  |= Tone |= Meaning |
  | <#d5e8d4> | Answers while the core is free-running |
  | <#dbe5f1> | A bounded read - refused while run = 1 |
  | <#e5d8f7> | A header field, at its native width |
  | <#ffe6cc> | The count ceiling - a contract with the host |
  | <#f8cecc> | A refusal, a fault, or the asymmetry between them |
endlegend

@enduml
